{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790254870,"nonce":"6DZe2J3TGtvzfJ3xOBVMxRQ3UAs=","title":"String length is a call into the string plugin, not a load","message":"zb_str_len binds $String$length in zrtl_string, an extern call, though a string is a pointer to an i32 length header followed by the bytes (null reads as 0). Lua's #s and Python's len(s) both lower to it, so a length in a loop is a foreign call per iteration that the inliner cannot see through.\n\nWhat would make it a load: a compiler-side lowering of the length of a String value (a BuiltinClass for String with len, or an intrinsic the builtins can name), emitting a null check and an i32 load sign-extended to i64 on every backend. The frontends keep calling zb_str_len by name and the builtin maps to it. Frontend code must not open-code the layout.","files":null}]}